# Logs
logs
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
lerna-debug.log*

node_modules
dist
dist-ssr
*.local
# Cargo build artifacts. The Cargo workspace lives at apps/desktop with
# target output at apps/desktop/target. Keeping target/ ignored also
# matters for biome, which honours the root .gitignore via
# `useIgnoreFile: true`, without this entry, biome scans compiled
# rustc_info.json + fingerprint files and floods the check with
# thousands of formatting complaints.
/apps/desktop/target
# Editor directories and files
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
.idea
.DS_Store
*.suo
*.ntvs*
*.njsproj
*.sln
*.sw?

# Other package managers' lockfiles. bun is the standard here (bun.lock
# is committed); yarn / npm / pnpm lockfiles should never be checked in
# because they'd fight the bun lockfile for source-of-truth. Tools like
# Next.js occasionally auto-install a fallback if their TS/eslint probe
# fails. This catches those artifacts before they can be committed.
yarn.lock
package-lock.json
pnpm-lock.yaml

# Signing and credential material, repeated at the root on purpose. The
# app that uses these ignores them already; this catches the same file
# dropped anywhere else in the tree, which is the case that actually
# happens. Extensions only, so no legitimate tracked config is caught.
*.jks
*.keystore
*.p8
*.p12
*.mobileprovision
keystore.properties
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
